{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "KAL Meet App — Auth & Kal",
    "description": "Smoke collection for Supabase JWT auth (KAL-004), `POST /kal` and `GET /kal/{id}`.\n\n## Setup\n1. `make up` (nginx on http://localhost:8080 by default).\n2. Have Supabase local running (`supabase start`) with a user that has a `profiles` row.\n3. Copy an access token from the FE / Supabase Auth (magic link session) into the collection variable `accessToken`, or into the **Local** environment.\n4. Set `baseUrl` if you use another port (`HTTP_PORT=8081` → `http://localhost:8081`).\n5. Run **POST /kal — create** first so `kalId` is set for the GET happy path.\n\n## Auth contract\n`Authorization: Bearer <supabase_jwt>`\n\n| Case | Status | `error` |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Missing / non-Bearer | 401 | `auth_token_missing` |\n| Bad signature / iss / aud | 401 | `auth_token_invalid` |\n| Expired | 401 | `auth_token_expired` |\n| Valid token, no profile | 401 | `auth_profile_not_found` |\n| JWKS unreachable (cold) | 503 | `auth_keys_unavailable` |\n\n`organizerId` must **not** appear in the body — it comes from the token.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
